                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ed35be8c-1939-30f3-905d-ca3dce127559",
                        "entry_id": "96b8347c-a317-3766-bb78-80a8c07e426e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Focused on one thing above all others."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "39bd183d-096d-494e-b26c-a62d0d654cea",
                                "sense_id": "ed35be8c-1939-30f3-905d-ca3dce127559",
                                "text": "...then it was that monomaniac Ahab, furious with this tantalizing vicinity of his foe, which placed him all alive and helpless in the very jaws he hated; frenzied with all this, he seized the long bone with his naked hands, and wildly strove to wrench it from its gripe."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "2edf2370-a4ee-3dd8-b0eb-cb0b2d306734",
                "word": "monomaniac",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "9248b632-aabf-4bb7-ac67-0b4cbb90ef32",
                        "entry_id": "2edf2370-a4ee-3dd8-b0eb-cb0b2d306734",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "monomaniacs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "af505cec-e4c7-364a-ac4e-f7c448e0b26f",
                        "entry_id": "2edf2370-a4ee-3dd8-b0eb-cb0b2d306734",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person who is obsessed with a single thing, to the exclusion of other concerns."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "65178ca5-af6c-483a-890e-5f4ff51d9229",
                                "sense_id": "af505cec-e4c7-364a-ac4e-f7c448e0b26f",
                                "text": "To talk nonsense, or poetry, or the dash between the two, in a tone of profound sincerity, and to enunciate solemn discordances with received opinion so seriously as to convey the impression of a spiritual insight, is the peculiar gift by which monomaniacs, having first persuaded themselves, contrive to influence their neighbours, and through them to make conquest of a good half of the world, for good or for ill."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b17bb12-67fe-4a90-8dc6-e6dc68064c7b",
                                "sense_id": "af505cec-e4c7-364a-ac4e-f7c448e0b26f",
                                "text": "Harry knew now that the old man was crazy, or at least a monomaniac, and, though he seemed harmless enough, it was of course possible that he might be dangerous."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b4138715-7b8e-44ad-b1ec-cde0c856cece",
                                "sense_id": "af505cec-e4c7-364a-ac4e-f7c448e0b26f",
                                "text": "He had never yet been able to determine whether the old man was a consummate hypocrite or a religious monomaniac."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1ebdf6e0-41bb-4c29-a1d1-344afd96e7ee",
                        "source_entry_id": "2edf2370-a4ee-3dd8-b0eb-cb0b2d306734",
                        "source_sense_id": "af505cec-e4c7-364a-ac4e-f7c448e0b26f",
                        "source_sense_description": "Translations",
                        "target_lang_word": "Monomane",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Monomane",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e7506fe0-f35e-31fb-a263-51ad8de40b6a",
                                        "entry_id": "50887ed8-babe-3227-a2a1-5fb3fb39b164",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Person, die an Monomanie leidet"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "407592f5-adf4-42a9-9614-20e983f62fca",
                                                "sense_id": "e7506fe0-f35e-31fb-a263-51ad8de40b6a",
                                                "text": "Als Monomane lebt er weitgehend unauffällig, nicht vergleichbar mit einem Wahnsinnigen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "350496bf-81e8-4e02-a4ad-b8ea6b95e1d9",
                                                "sense_id": "e7506fe0-f35e-31fb-a263-51ad8de40b6a",
                                                "text": "„Er war auch ein Monomane der Bagatelle, vorausgesetzt daß sie sein Wohlbefinden anging.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a0e29e29-ce9c-49f4-9458-dfb73be13dd4",
                        "source_entry_id": "2edf2370-a4ee-3dd8-b0eb-cb0b2d306734",
                        "source_sense_id": "af505cec-e4c7-364a-ac4e-f7c448e0b26f",
